schema: test/v2
level: working-unit
epic: E-REDESIGN
wu: E-REDESIGN.W8
branch: wu/redesign/body-viewer-build
tests:
  unit:
    count: 23
    detail: "ui/src/BodyViewer.test.tsx REWRITTEN to the new contract — 21 tests, where the old file had 16. The rewrite is deliberate and is itself evidence: the old file asserted a <details> tree, leg tabs and a 'copied' that never reverts, and all three are defects this WU removes, so every deleted assertion maps to a design line that deleted it. Coverage: the leg prop drives the fetch and NO leg control exists in the pane; six dispatch cases each asserting the MEMBER's own testid (body-json as a CodeMirror surface with no <details>, body-xml — asserted for the first time in the repo, body-text, body-hex, body-form with per-pair copy targets, body-image); raw mode refetches undecoded and dispatches through rawKind; three truncation paths (text over TEXT_MAX, hex over HEX_MAX, json over TREE_MAX falling back with the marker), each asserting the two sizes in the marker DIFFER rather than merely that a marker exists; copy yields valid JSON (the payload is fed to JSON.parse) and the hex dump for hex; the confirm reverts after CONFIRM_MS under fake timers; an image offers save but no copy; save writes ALL the bytes (the Blob size is asserted against the full body, not the shown 128 KiB) which is what makes the cut marker's advice true; and the seven zone states with data-tone asserted, warn on the failure alone plus an assertion that no retry control exists. ui/src/body.test.ts +2 — the too-large notice states a human size, and the null-size case states no size at all rather than '0 B'."
  integration:
    count: 2
    detail: "ui/src/FlowDetail.test.tsx +2, asserting the WU's bounded contract — the one thing no unit test can reach, because it is about two instances coexisting. (1) The panel mounts one pane per leg: a Request body and a Response body section both render, both panes reach body-text, and getBody is called for BOTH legs. (2) Each pane owns its own mode: clicking the request pane's raw segment refetches request/decode=0 and the response leg's calls do not move — the property that replaced the leg switch, and the one a shared-state regression would break silently."
  e2e:
    count: 3
    detail: "ui/e2e/specs/flows.spec.ts +3, plus 2 new origin routes in ui/e2e/harness/main.rs. The two contracts the epic plan names as UC-5's NEW ones, proven against the real proxy, the real API and the real Tauri window: 'renders an XML body as XML, not as fall-through text' (/xml serves application/xml; the response pane reaches body-xml and body-text is asserted ABSENT) and 'states its truncation on a body past the render cap' (/big serves 200000 bytes of text/plain — past the UI's 128 KiB render cap, far under the 10 MiB capture cap, so the body is captured whole and the pane must state what it left out). Plus 'shows both legs at once, each under its own heading'. Hermetic: the harness's own local HTTPS origin on an ephemeral port, no public network."
verified:
  - "cd ui && pnpm test — 536 passed / 42 files, 0 failed. The base (epic/redesign) is 527, so this WU is +9 net after replacing 16 old BodyViewer tests with 21. The nine BodyRenderer family component tests that ship from W2 all stayed green as their first real consumer arrived — the point of the whole swap is that the screen stopped re-implementing what they already assert."
  - "cargo xtask ui e2e — 13 passing, 0 failing across both spec files (4 onboarding + 9 inspect). Both new UC-5 contracts pass. Run twice: the first run found two of MY assertions wrong (an invalid compound WebDriver selector, and expecting getText to return the CSS-uppercased heading), not two product defects — both fixed in the spec, and the product code was not touched to make a test pass."
  - "cd ui && pnpm exec eslint src — clean, including the closed-vocabulary lint. Worth stating because the pane's one sizing class was nearly a fabricated token: the first draft wrote max-h-body-pane, which does not exist. The real token is the existing spacing member body-max (256px), which already had a consumer in Gallery.tsx. No literal, no new token, no config change."
  - "cd ui && pnpm exec tsc --noEmit — clean. Note that tsc is what proved the leg prop is genuinely required rather than defaulted: making it required turned every old call site into a compile error, which is how the old test file's 16 call sites were found."
  - "cargo test — 7 suites, all ok, 0 failed. cargo clippy --all-targets and cargo fmt --check — clean (the pre-commit hook ran both on all three commits). The Rust change is the e2e harness's two origin routes; it compiles and the harness binary builds."
  - "The marker this WU was assigned to close is closed: grep across ui/src/ for JsonNode, JsonTree, TextBody, FormBody, ImageBody, ModeButton and 'E-DFLOW.W5 Q2' returns NOTHING. BodyViewer.tsx went 238 -> 129 lines."
  - "The design's three do-not rules were checked as code facts, not as intentions. (1) 'Every cap is the member's own, and the caller sets none of them' — BodyViewer.tsx imports no TEXT_MAX/HEX_MAX/TREE_MAX and passes no threshold to any member. (2) 'C carries no mount in this screen's tree' — no CutMarker import; the screen's only truncation duty is the bounded scroll box the Tune stage called for. (3) 'No retry affordance' — no action prop on any of the seven Notices, and a unit test asserts no retry control exists, so a later edit that adds one goes red rather than passing quietly."
  - "The one place the build did NOT transcribe the plan is recorded rather than smoothed over: bodyNotice's actual is number | null, so humanBytes(actual ?? 0) would render 'not captured — too large (0 B)' — a false size in the one component whose job is true ones. The build wrote two sentences instead of one and tests both; the deviation is in the result report."
  - "cargo xtask verify-doc green on all four docs touched: the W8 plan (wu-plan), the W8 result (wu-result), the epic plan (epic-plan) after its W8 and W6 blocks were corrected, and web-ui.html (ungoverned — link check only)."
  - "Review round 2, after the two fixes: cd ui && pnpm test 536 passed / 42 files; eslint and tsc clean; cargo xtask ui e2e 13 passing / 0 failing again, both new UC-5 contracts included. The CopyButton value prop was removed and the e2e suite re-run because the pane's JSX changed."
  - "The one review fix worth naming in a test note, because it is about evidence rather than code: the review's own verifier refuted the eager-value finding by probing CopyButton in isolation, concluding the prop was load-bearing for the confirm reset. It is not, at THIS call site — setFetched(null) on every mode/leg change unmounts the whole action group, so the confirm cannot survive a payload change with or without it. Established by deleting the prop and re-running the suite: it stayed green, which proved the test written to guard the prop could not fail and so was not evidence. The test now asserts the invariant that actually holds (unmount clears the confirm), and was re-checked the same way."
